    "result_text": "The full suite is green. The change is complete and verified.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field. The audit log confirms the new format: `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (NSW region + `27` fiscal year + `16E6609E` HASH8 + `1` Luhn check digit).\n\n**Identity/derivation logic**\n- `OwnerIdentities.java` \u2014 replaced `customerCode()` with `memberId()`, which composes `REGION + FY + HASH8` and appends a single Luhn `CHK` over that base's digits. Extracted a private `hash8()` helper (the same SHA-256-over-`normalizedTelephone+lastName` first-8-hex). `primaryIdentifier()` now returns `getMemberId()`.\n- `CheckDigits.java` \u2014 dropped `checkDigitFor(Owner)` (the removed `checkDigit` field); kept `luhn()`, now used for the CHK segment.\n\n**Entity, DTO, persistence**\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 removed `customerCode`/`membershipNumber` fields + accessors; added `memberId` (`member_id` column).\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed `customerCode`, `checkDigit`, `membershipNumber` schemas; added a `memberId` schema (MapStruct auto-maps it by name).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 removed the `checkDigit` mapping.\n- All four `schema.sql` dialects (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 replaced the two columns with `member_id`.\n\n**Pipeline & behaviour changes required by the spec**\n- **Collision handling \u2192 memberId**: replaced `AssignCustomerCode`/`AssignMembershipNumber` with a single `AssignMemberId` step (updated `owners.POST.yml`), which de-dupes against existing `memberId`s (appending `-<n>`).\n- **Fiscal-year value \u2192 memberId**: the FY (2-digit fiscal year) is now the FY segment inside `memberId`.\n- **Audit record \u2192 memberId**: `OwnerCreatedEvent`'s field renamed `customerCode`\u2192`memberId`; `RespondWithOwnerCreated` logs `memberId`.\n- **Owner segment \u2192 memberId**: `Localities.localityFor(Owner)` now derives the region from the `memberId` prefix (leading letters up to the FY digits) instead of the removed `customerCode`, feeding `OwnerSegments`.\n\nI also updated the dangling javadoc `@link`s in `ResolveRegistrationDate` and `CheckCityCapacity`. Both the targeted `AcceptanceTest` and the full `./mvnw test` suite pass (`BUILD SUCCESS`).",
